SUMMARY:The Desert\, the Mystic\, the Musician
DESCRIPTION:Some of the desert’s oldest songs live in the voices of a single community. This interactive session is an introduction to the musical heritage of the Mirs from Pugal\, Rajasthan. The evening beings with an audio-visual storytelling journey through the desert landscape\, setting the scene for the musical performance by three generations of Mirasi musicians. \nDrawing on the songs of the desert mystics across languages and folk practices\, the music spans the Bhakti and Sufi traditions. From Saraiki songs to those sung in regional dialects\, this slowly fading tradition carries the sounds of the land and the stories of its people. \nCredits: \nStorytelling & Curation: Meghal Sharma\nVocals & Harmonium: Rajak Ali\nVocals\, Tabla & Algoza: Abdul Jabbar\nTabla: Rahul\nPercussion: Shahrukh \nSupported by: \n \nVenue: Seminar Halls\n\n\nMusic of the Mirs\nRSVP here (https://docs.google.com/forms/d/e/1FAIpQLSee7nS6MCV0EwhBNcszG-po3S-G3hS9AxyVncTCM7LhW63QJw/viewform?usp=publish-editor)\n*Performers*: Rajak Ali\, Abdul Jabbar\, Meghal Sharma\n*Event Categories*: Music\, Performing Arts
URL:https://bangaloreinternationalcentre.org/event/the-desert-the-mystic-the-musician/
LOCATION:Bangalore International Centre\, 7\, 4th Main Road\, Domlur II Stage\, Bangalore\, Karnataka\, 560071\, India
CATEGORIES:Music,Performing Arts
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://bangaloreinternationalcentre.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/Thumbnail-1.jpg
