SUMMARY:Miracle in Antarctica
DESCRIPTION:70 min | English with English subtitles | 2026 | India \nIn December 1983\, geophysicist and seismologist Dr. Harsh Kumar Gupta is sent to Antarctica to lead an impossible mission: build Dakshin Gangotri\, India’s first scientific base station\, before the end of the Antarctic summer. Given a fleeting timeframe of barely sixty days\, success would set a world record. Alas\, time is not his only adversary. After a blizzard and a helicopter crash\, can determination outpace the pack ice? \nThe screening of the film will be followed by a discussion with the protagonist and filmmakers. A Q&A with the audience will follow. \nPresented by: \n          \nVenue: Auditorium\n\n\nThe Forgotten Story of Dakshin Gangotri\nRSVP here (https://docs.google.com/forms/d/e/1FAIpQLSeZ5okx8VgNFN2sNFRsPV-t6LiQ2_PKvtu3JQ3u0iOfk2k7KA/viewform?usp=publish-editor)\n*Speakers*: Santosh Saligram\, Sourabha Rao\, Harsh Kumar Gupta\, Suraj Sumanth\, Preeti Zachariah\n*Event Categories*: Film\, Science
URL:https://bangaloreinternationalcentre.org/event/miracle-in-antarctica/
LOCATION:Bangalore International Centre\, 7\, 4th Main Road\, Domlur II Stage\, Bangalore\, Karnataka\, 560071\, India
CATEGORIES:Film,Science
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://bangaloreinternationalcentre.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/Thumbnailoct-28.jpg
